       buffer,  which  subsequent  calls will overwrite.  eetthheerr__aattoonn() returns
       NULL if the address is invalid.

       The eetthheerr__nnttooaa() function converts the Ethernet host address _a_d_d_r given
       in network byte order to a string in standard hex‐digits‐and‐colons no‐
       tation, omitting leading zeros.  The string is returned in a statically
       allocated buffer, which subsequent calls will overwrite.

       The eetthheerr__nnttoohhoosstt() function maps an Ethernet  address  to  the  corre‐
       sponding  hostname  in  _/_e_t_c_/_e_t_h_e_r_s and returns nonzero if it cannot be
       found.

       The eetthheerr__hhoossttttoonn() function maps a hostname to the corresponding  Eth‐
